<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n41127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕ-nŭmĕro</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum, 1, v. a.
		(anteand post-class.). <b>Lit.</b>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to count over</i>,
				<i>count up.</i> — Hence, transf., <i>to pay back</i>, <i>repay</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurum alicui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Bacch. 1, 1, 12</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 4, 18</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnem pecuniam patri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 2, 26</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dotem huc,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Hec. 3, 5, 52</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pecuniam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 332, 25</span></i>
			.</div>
